      "reason": "Out of budget before writing or evaluating a change; nothing was submitted. The code is already heavily optimised. Best remaining lead (an estimate, not measured): train_ir. Both train loops copy and scan every pair count on each merge step to find the top pair. A lazily checked heap of (-count, pair), pushing each changed pair once per merge and keeping the existing chunk scan to break ties, should keep output byte-identical and cut that cost a lot."
